# **This is the only `.dockerignore` that is read.**
#
# Both images build with the repo root as their context, and Docker looks for `.dockerignore` at
# the *context* root — not beside the Dockerfile. `apps/web/.dockerignore` and
# `apps/api/.dockerignore` are inert, which is why the host's `node_modules` was reaching the web
# image and colliding with the flat tree installed inside it: pnpm's store is symlinks, the image's
# is real directories, and Docker cannot replace one with the other.

.git/
.github/

# Node
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/coverage/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/blob-report/
apps/web/e2e/.auth/
apps/web/e2e/.fixtures.json

# Python
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage

# Secrets and local state. `.env` is mounted at run time, never baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env.local

# Docs and scratch
*.md
!apps/api/README.md
*.png
